For almost 4 months I have been playing on and off on NAO (stupermon),
trying to ascend all classes.

Currently, I just finished 'clearing' the VotD with a Valk, the last
class that I haven't ascended, but I am rather bored and can't seem to
decide to spend a couple of days to finish that last game.

http://alt.org/nethack/player-all.php?player=stupermon

I thought I would give a quick breakdown of how it went for me: - BTW -
sometimes when trying to start a new game, I would accidentally hit
space or enter and get a random character choice that I didn't wish to
play , so I would quit on the first move.  I don't count those
accidents when counting consecutive ascensions.

Started off by getting killed twice - once as a caveman and once as a
wizard.

Then I ascended three times in a row - Ranger, Wizard, and Caveman.  I
then decided to start doing the classes in alphabetical order.

This was followed by two Arc deaths, an Dwarven Arc ascension, a
Barbarian YAAD to a /WoDeath followed by an orcish Barbarian ascension,
three failed healers before I finally ascended a gnomish healer.  Two
failed Knights followed by a female Knight ascension,  Monk and Elven
priest ascensions on the first try, a failed orcish rogue followed by a
female orcish rogue ascension, another /WoDeath YAAD on a Samurai
before I ascended one, two failed tourists followed by another
ascension, and my current Valk, who appears to be ready to ascend on
the first try.

So here's the stats:
Acended on first try:
Monk, Priest, Ranger, and (hopefully) Valk

Ascended on second try:
Barbarian, Caveman, Rogue, Samurai, Wizard

Third times the charm:
Arc, Knight, Tourist

Four attempts required: Healer

Longest ascension streak - 3(twice) - Ranger, Wizard, Caveman and
Knight, Monk, Priest

So that means I will have ascended 13 classes in 27 games, just over
48% success rate.

All games were genocide-less.  Some were wishless, most were
polyselfless.

Trying to come up with something interesting to do with the rest of the
game so I can finish this Valk.

Happy Hacking

